      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt from \u0027\u003Ci\u003EThe English Cookery Book\u003C/i\u003E\u0027 edited by JH Walsh \u003Ca href=\u0022references.html#walsh-1859\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003EWalsh 1859\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E;",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003ENovice\u0027s Pudding.\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\n955. Beat well the whites of eight eggs, and mix with them half a pound of loaf-sugar by degrees. Stir the mixture into a pint of good milk (flavoured with vanilla or sherry) alternately with four ounces of flour, a spoonful at a time; beat it very hard, put it in rather a quick oven, and bake it well. Serve cold.\u003Cbr\u003E"
